{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["And the reason for <b>Command the children of Israel and say to them: My offering, my bread</b> — for after it said \"to these the land shall be divided,\" He commanded to complete the law of the offerings that they shall do thus in the land, for in the wilderness they did not offer the additional offerings (מוספים) as I mentioned in the section of \"Speak to the priests\" (Leviticus 23:2), and likewise they were not obligated in libations (נסכים) in the wilderness, as I explained in the section of \"Send for yourself\" (Ramban on Numbers 15:2). And now He obligated the people of the land to do everything there — the daily offerings (תמידין) and the additional offerings (מוספין) and their meal-offering and their libations. And even though He did not specify here \"when you come into the land,\" He already mentioned it in the section of the libations (ibid.) and alluded to it in the first section on the festivals (Leviticus 23:10). And He began here with the daily offering, even though it was mentioned in the section of \"And you shall command\" (Exodus 29:38); He repeated it so that everything would be arranged in one section. And Rashi wrote (Rashi on Numbers 28:4): this was a warning for the days of consecration (מילואים), and here He commanded for the generations. And this is not correct, for there it says \"a continual burnt-offering throughout your generations.\" And according to the midrash, many things were renewed here: \"My offering\" — this is the blood; \"my bread\" — these are the emurim (fatty portions); \"for My fire-offerings\" (לאשי) — these are the fistfuls (קמצין) and the frankincense; \"a pleasing fragrance\" — these are the arrangements of the showbread. \"You shall keep\" (תשמרו) — that he should not bring except from what is guarded; \"you shall keep\" — that he should not bring except from the chamber's terumah; \"you shall keep\" — that there should be priests and Levites and Israelites standing over it; \"you shall keep\" — guarding is said here and guarding is said further on — just as further on it is inspected for four days before its slaughter, so too here, etc. And the entire midrash is as it is in Sifrei. And by way of truth, it alludes to them further and says, <b>\"My offering, my food, for My fire-offerings\"</b> — that which is of fire-offerings you shall keep and be careful to offer it to Me for My name at its appointed time. And you shall say to them further <b>\"this is the fire-offering which you shall offer to YHWH\"</b> — that the offering should be brought near. There is no sin-offering among the additional offerings of the Sabbath as in all the other additional offerings, because Knesset Israel is His counterpart and all is peace, and the enlightened will understand. And likewise He mentioned: <b>\"And in the first month, on the fourteenth day of the month, is the Passover to YHWH\"</b> (Numbers 28:16) — that they should make the Passover offering, to warn concerning it along with the rest of the offerings of the Festival of Unleavened Bread, and He was brief concerning it, to mention its name alone, for He had already explained its law with all its statutes and all its judgments."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:09:28.697869078Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}